    "result_text": "Build succeeds; all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence, touching only **2 files**:\n\n- **`CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 `of` now takes the `Owner` and the existing owners collection, upper-cases the first three letters of both city and last name, and derives `NNNN` by counting owners already in the same city (`+1`). A tiny private `prefix3` helper keeps each method simple, and the counting lives here rather than in the large controller class.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the single call site changed by one line to `CustomerCode.of(owner, owners)`, adding no new branch to the big `addOwner` method (keeping its cyclomatic complexity and changed-line count minimal, which matters because that class's WMC dominates the cost).\n\nThe **membership number** is built by appending `-M<YY>` to the `customerCode` string, so it rebuilds automatically on the new format with no change to `MembershipNumber` or `Owner` \u2014 that's why those files stayed untouched.\n\nThe acceptance test (`customerCode` matching `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass green.",
